# Documentation builds
# `site/` is the documentation site's tracked source, not its build output: MkDocs writes to
# `build/site` (covered by the `build/` rule above), because its default output directory is `site/`,
# which would build the site on top of its own source and hide `site.md` from every commit.
docs/_build/
# Two pages are generated by site/scripts/build.py from other content, so they are not committed:
# the roadmap is derived from the pages' own front matter, and `reference/` is a copy of `docs/`.
site/roadmap.md
site/reference/
